<title>DUBAI: Abu Dhabi approves petrochemical plant.</title>
<headline>Abu Dhabi approves petrochemical plant.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Gulf Arab emirate of Abu Dhabi has officially approved plans to set up a 450,000 tonnes a year plastics plant in a joint venture with Scandinavia's Borealis, the official Emirates News Agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the Supreme Petroleum Council approved the building of the plant at a meeting on Sunday night.</p>
<p>Abu Dhabi National Oil Company (ADNOC) in July signed a memorandum of understanding (MOU) with Borealis to build the ethane-based ethylene cracker and polyethylene plant at Ruwais.</p>
<p>Industry sources estimate the new petrochemical plant will cost between $1 billion and $1.5 billion.</p>
<p>Borealis is a 50-50 chemicals joint venture between Finland's Neste Oy and Norway's Den Norske Stats Oljeselskap AS (Statoil).</p>
<p>The project is expected to go onstream in the year 2000.</p>
</text>
